    <DataNode elementId="AT5G46180-MONOMER" textLabel="ornithine-δ-aminotransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9FNK4" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; cDNA of gene &lt;i&gt;&amp;delta;-OAT&lt;/i&gt; has been isolated based on sequence similarity with ornithine-&amp;delta;-aminotransferases from yeast, mammal, plant and bacterial sequences. OAT activity has been found in extracts from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; plants |CITS:[9576796]|, and plants bearing a mutation in the &lt;i&gt;&amp;delta;-OAT&lt;/i&gt; gene have severely reduced levels of OAT activity |CITS: [18419821]|. Conversely, plants over-expressing this enzyme have elevated levels of OAT activity |CITS: [18419821]|. Transcriptional analyses of this gene indicate that it is upregulated in young tissue and in response to salt stress |CITS: [9576796]|. The mitochondrial location of this enzyme and the phenotype of mutant plants suggests that it is not involved in proline biosynthesis, but likely plays a role in arginine catabolism |CITS: [18419821]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G46180-MONOMER" />
